.                                                    AN OSCAR, OSCAR

The great German actress Brunhilda Von Divagruber had achieved =
everything she wanted in life but for one honor: She'd never won an =
Academy Award.

One day she was called by the great director Meyer Schmidtenlager and =
asked to review a new script he had. She read the script and immediately =
rejected it. "Iss nicht my type of script, Meyer, and I'll not do it."

"But honeykins," he cried, "it's a wonderful script."

"I didn't say it vasn't vunderful or goot, but I'll not do it."

"But sweetiekins," Meyer continued, "with my direction and your acting =
and name, the film will make us millions."

"More geldt I don't need. Ich do nicht like the script."

"But, darling, don't you see? With my connections, I can almost =
guarantee you an Academy Award for your performance."

Brunhilda thought a moment then agreed, musing, "Oh, I'd luff to be an =
Oscar winner, Meyer!"

